{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"87423","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/87423","key":"MC-195572","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"20/Jul/20 7:36 AM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<h3><a name=\"TheBug%3A\"></a><b>The Bug:</b></h3>\n\n<p>The fog from lava is much denser in java edition when having the fire resistance effect active compared to bedrock edition.</p>\n<h3><a name=\"StepstoReproduce%3A\"></a><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b></h3>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Launch the java edition version of the game and join a world.</li>\n\t<li>Drink a fire resistance potion and enter a large area of lava.</li>\n\t<li>Take note of how dense the lava fog is.</li>\n\t<li>Launch the bedrock edition version of the game and join a world.</li>\n\t<li>Drink a fire resistance potion and enter a large area of lava.</li>\n\t<li>Take note of how dense the lava fog is compared to java edition.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<h3><a name=\"ObservedBehavior%3A\"></a><b>Observed Behavior:</b></h3>\n\n<p>The fog from lava is much denser in java edition when having the fire resistance effect active compared to bedrock edition.</p>\n<h3><a name=\"ExpectedBehavior%3A\"></a><b>Expected Behavior:</b></h3>\n\n<p>The fog from lava in java and bedrock edition when having the fire resistance effect active would have the same density.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"20/Jul/20 3:14 PM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/113493","id":"113493","filename":"2020-07-20_16.33.51.png","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d70168bc4d0c82762f0a18f8b5637505?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.pro